label mac_season2_episode4:

    $tbc = False
    scene hifl_prologue at bg
    play music hifleveryday

    pause
    $hidetextbox = True
    $ renpy.block_rollback()
    $hideborders = False

    "Razi recovers first, adjusting the collar of the newly reappeared shirt."

    ra "Werewolves? You sure about that?"

    jd "She’s not human, Razi. It’s fine."

    "(How can they tell?  She looks like any other girl to me.)"

    "Mackenzie steps away from me, the mask of the sheriff falling across her face."

    "It’s like the playfulness from a moment before was never there at all."

    ma "Let’s start from the beginning."
    ma "What’s your name?"
    unknown "Gwen."
    gwe "This is Havenfall, right? Because I heard you protect people here."
    jd "We protect each other."
    jd "Who exactly is after you?"
    gwe "The Rider pack."
    "Anger glitters like something sharp in Mackenzie’s eyes, her hands clenching into fists."
    ma "There’s a lot of Riders out there. Which ones?"
    gwe "The alpha. I don’t know his name, but he..."
    "Gwen trembles in open terror, and I remember seeing the exact same look on Damien’s face."
    "(So much for staying out of Mac’s territory. Beau’s already trying to cause trouble!)"
    ma "Beau. His name is Beau Rider."
    "I move a little closer to Gwen, wanting to offer some sympathy."
    mcmac "Are you a rogue wolf too?"
    ra "[genericfn], you can’t ask that."
    "I’ve heard Razi get annoyed before—mostly at customers trying to skip their bar tab—but the hardness in his voice is a step beyond that"
    mcmac "Sorry, I didn’t mean to assume."
    "My startled apology makes Razi’s shoulders relax, and he smiles."
    ra "It’s okay."
    ra "Just understand that it’s not safe for everyone to...disclose. We try not to ask each other unless it’s absolutely necessary."
    "(Considering what I’ve seen of werewolf politics, that makes sense.)"
    "(It doesn’t matter what Gwen is. What’s important is that Beau’s threatening her.)"
    di "Are you injured, Gwen?"
    gwe "No, just out of breath. But I don’t know what he wants from me."
    gwe "I’m not even local."
    "I can’t place her accent, but it’s hard to focus on that when I see the storm of emotion playing out across Mackenzie’s face."
    "It’s not just anger, it’s grave offence."
    ma "If a werewolf is after you, it’s my problem."
    ma "So give me a minute to discuss things with everyone else, okay?"
    "Gwen nods, and Mackenzie jerks her head over towards the bar."

    "Diego follows first, but JD and Razi are close behind, breaking into a hushed conversation as soon as they’re all close together."

    "(I’ll make sure Gwen doesn’t feel left out.)"
    mcmac "Let’s sit down, okay? You must be exhausted."
    gwe "Kind of. It feels like I’ve been running for hours."
    "She folds herself into one of our cheap chairs, and I take a seat next to her."
    mcmac "How old are you?"
    gwe "Eighteen. As of a week ago, anyway."
    gwe "Being an adult already sucks."
    mcmac "I feel you there."
    mcmac "Do you have any family? A place to go?"
    "Gwen shakes her head, eyes dropping down to the floor."
    $menuhideborder = True
    menu macs2e4c1:
        "A. Ask more questions.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "Did you run here?"
            gwe "Yeah. No car."
            gwe "Which I’m regretting right about now."

        "B. Give her a break.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            "(She doesn’t need me interrogating her after being chased down.)"
            mcmac "Don’t worry about it."
            mcmac "Just sit here and catch your breath."

        "C. Try to be welcoming.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "Well, Havenfall's not a bad place to stop."
            mcmac "You'll definitely be safe here."
            "(I wonder if Razi kept the wards up from when Damien tried to get in.)"

    "Mackenzie breaks away from the group at the bar and comes over to us, her face locked in a serious expression"
    ma "I don’t know what Beau might have told you, Gwen, but this is my territory."
    ma "He can’t hurt you here. I won’t let him."
    gwe "But he’s still out there somewhere."
    ma "I know, but I’ll be taking care of that."
    gwe "T-Thank you."

    "The friendly smile I know and love curves Mackenzie’s mouth, breaking through the tension in the room."
    "Whether she’s acting as sheriff or alpha, the protective steak never fades."
    ma "Come on. We’ll lay down the ground rules for you."
    mcmac "Ground rules?"
    ra "Like where she’s staying, first and foremost."
    ra "I can ward this building, Gwen, so you’d be best off staying upstairs with JD and I, alright?"
    gwe "Okay. If it’s not too much trouble."
    jd "Ignore all the noise from Razi’s room."
    jd "It’s just him watching his dramas."
    "Razi rolls his eyes, but the joke makes Gwen smile, and she looks better for it."
    ma "The next is that you can’t reveal yourself to anyone, Gwen."
    ma "I don’t need to know your background, but the humans here can’t either. Got it?"
    gwe "No worries."
    gwe "I mean, it’s that way pretty much everywhere."
    jd "No using your abilities on anyone else either. Sheriff’s not a fan of that."
    "JD raises their hands up in mock surrender when Mackenzie shoots them a look, but the tension doesn’t stick."

    "The two of them know each other too well."
    gwe "I won’t, I promise."
    ma "Is there anything else you can tell us about what happened?"
    gwe "You’ll think I’m stupid."
    "Shame twists like a sour note through Gwen’s voice, and I lay a gentle hand on her shoulder."

    "Open surprise flicker’s through her eyes, but she doesn’t pull away."
    mcmac "Whatever happened, it’s not your fault."
    gwe "I was hitchhiking."
    gwe "It’s such a stereotype to run away the second you turn legal, but I wanted out. I wanted to see the world."
    gwe "Then this truck slowed down by me, and the guy inside rolled his window down."
    gwe "I didn’t realise what he was. I should have."
    ma "What proved it?"
    gwe "Those teeth. His eyes right after the change."
    gwe "I’ve never run so fast in my life."
    "(Jesus, is that how Beau gets his kicks? Terrifying people with nowhere to go??)"
    "I can tell Mackenzie’s livid, but doing her best to tamp it down."

    "Revealing her rage would probably bring the wolf with it, and that’s the last thing Gwen needs right now."
    ra "How about we talk more in the morning?"
    ra "Let’s get you upstairs, Gwen. I’ll make up a bed and a bite to eat."
    jd "Yeah. His cooking’s pretty good too."
    "JD helps Gwen to her feet, and the three of them head out the back door of the bowling alley up to Razi’s place."

    "As soon as the door swings shut, Mackenzie lets out a deep, shaking breath."
    mcmac "Hey. Come here."
    "She does, and Mackenzie’s arm comes around my back, bringing me close."
    "Once the contact settles between us, the anger bleeds away from her gaze, and I wait until she’s ready to talk."
    ma "Beau’s trying to provoke me."
    ma "Worse, it’s already working."
    mcmac "Is it safe to keep Gwen here? I mean, is he going to attack us to get to her?"
    ma "I don’t know, but it doesn’t matter."
    ma "Havenfall is mine to protect. So are all the people here, especially the ones seeking refuge."

    $menuhideborder = True
    menu macs2e4c2:
        "A. I know you'll keep her safe.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "I know you’ll keep her safe, Mac."
            mcmac "Without you, I don’t think I’d have survived Damien, much less someone like Beau."
            ma "I don’t want Beau near you either."

        "B. I'm right here with you.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "I'm right here with you."
            ma "I'd say 'birds of a feather', but neither one of us have those."
            mcmac "No, although your furry ears are pretty cute."

        "C. Even if it puts you at risk?":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "Even if it puts you at risk?"
            ma "My job puts me at risk. Even if werewolf business wasn’t involved, I would be as sheriff."
            ma "The danger’s part of the package. It doesn’t bother me."

    "(What does Beau even get out of this? Is he just trying to intimidate Mac?)"

    "The worry must show on my face, because Mackenzie turns just enough to look me in the eye."
    ma "[genericfn], I’m the law here."
    ma "Sometimes that means enforcing it. Another alpha with an ego the size of Texas doesn’t change that."
    mcmac "He’s real bad news, Mac. I feel it in my gut."
    ma "Then it’s up to me to be the good, isn’t it?"
    ma "It’s up to us."
    "The ‘us’ makes me smile, and Mackenzie pulls me into a full hug."
    "With my face pressed against her chest, I can hear the solid, relentless beat of her heart."
    "With Beau still lurking around Havenfall, Mackenzie asks me to come home with her."
    "I’m more than happy to, and right after she locks the door, I already feel a little better."
    ma "Sorry we had to break up the party."
    ma "You want something to eat? It’d fend off the hangover."
    mcmac "I had so much cake. Eating more might make me sick anyway."
    mcmac "But I’ll take water."
    "She leaves me by the bedroom while getting glasses out of the kitchen, and I kick off my shoes, vest, and hat before settling at the end of Mackenzie’s bed."

    "I hit the sheets with a light thump, looking up at the ceiling and then back a little further."

    "(Those are some serious bars across her window.)"
    "(Are those to keep other werewolves out or...her in?)"

    "The door swinging open breaks my train of thought, and I feel my face heat up when Mackenzie leans over me to offer a cool glass."
    ma "Getting comfortable?"
    mcmac "It’s not my fault your bed is really nice."
    ma "Well, I’m glad. You’ll be staying in it a while."
    "She realised what she’s just said a second later, and quietly coughs before sitting down on the other side of the bed."
    ma "You want to watch a movie? Something to take our mind off things."
    mcmac "You don’t have a TV in here."
    ma "No, but I can stream whatever on my laptop. It’ll be cozy."
    "(There’s no way I’m refusing that invitation.)"
    "I gulp down the water while Mackenzie strips out of her uniform, locking her gun away before slipping into bed with me."
    "Our legs brush under the blanket while she moves the computer up onto her lap."
    ma "What are you in the mood for?"
    mcmac "Pick your favorite."
    mcmac "Usually I watch documentaries, but they tend to knock me out."
    "Mackenzie smiles, clicking around for a minute before making her decision."

    "The preview image has a woman in armor lifting a tank up over her head."

    "(I’m already interested.)"
    mcmac "If this is a superhero movie, you’ll have to give me the backstory."
    ma "Don’t worry, I will."
    "The film opens up on a beautiful island, and I’m appreciating the scenery when the clatter of sandals and weapons booms from the speakers."

    "There’s too many women fighting onscreen to count, and one of them does a flip that makes jaw drop."
    ma "Killer stunt work, right?"
    mcmac "No kidding."
    ma "It’s a pretty big deal, actually. Stuntwomen have risky jobs because most ladies in action movie are, well..."
    mcmac "Not wearing very much?"
    ma "Yeah. It’s hard to hide padding in a bikini."
    mcmac "You’d be good at doing stunts."
    mcmac "I mean, you’re not just fit, you heal faster than other people."
    ma "Probably less exhausting than getting in real fights too."
    ma "Ooh, look! Okay, so that character is a reference to the one in the comic..."
    "Mackenzie’s whole face lights up as she starts explaining the different connections, pointing to the screen to make sure I don’t mix up any names."
    "Even details in the props don’t escape her attention, and I’m amazed at how much she knows."
    ma "...But Silver and Golden age stuff is always a little wild anyway."
    "She pauses, cheeks warming with embarrassment."
    ma "I can knock off the commentary if I’m going overboard."
    mcmac "No way. I signed up for the director’s cut."
    mcmac "It’s adorable, Mac. Really."
    "I kiss one blushing cheek to make my point known, but Mackenzie still looks pretty flustered."
